# (build 111) The AUDIO page's EFFECTS: the sequencer's hooks tell a sound
# effect's writes from the music's, so MUSIC turns the music alone down and
# EFFECTS the effects. On the chip an effect plays on a channel it takes
# from the music (FM3-FM5); the channels an effect last struck are weighted
# by EFFECTS, the rest by MUSIC, clock by clock (docs/audio.md, "The
# hooks"). With `sound render on` the probe renders each tick's audio at the
# page's volumes, as main.c hands them to the mixer.
#
# On the title with its theme playing: MUSIC OFF and the mix is silent;
# Gaj ($C1, a technique's sound, 32 ticks on FM3, FM4 and FM5) queued over
# it plays at EFFECTS 0 dB -- before 111 MUSIC silenced it too, and there
# was no EFFECTS row nor `sound play`; then EFFECTS OFF and Gaj again is
# silent; then MUSIC back to 0 dB with EFFECTS still OFF, and the theme
# plays. The page, a row taller, drawn for a look.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
expect sound playing
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
expect audio effects 0 DB
press down
press down
press c
expect audio music OFF
wait ticks 40
expect sound silent
sound play $C1
wait ticks 10
expect sound playing
wait ticks 60
expect sound silent
press down
press c
expect audio effects OFF
wait ticks 8
shot page_effects_off
sound play $C1
wait ticks 10
expect sound silent
wait ticks 40
press up
press c
expect audio music -30 DB
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
press right
expect audio music 0 DB
wait ticks 30
expect sound playing
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
